<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nasir Khan Faruqi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1399–1437</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nasir Khan Faruqi was the second ruler of the Faruqi dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khandesh">Khandesh</a> in the Tapti valley of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, reigning from 1399 to 1437. He captured the hill fortress of Asirgarh and founded the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burhanpur">Burhanpur</a>, which became the Faruqi capital. His reign was marked by conflict with the neighbouring Bahmani and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> sultanates.</p></div>
